<!-- awf:section positioning -->
# {{ .prefix }}-proposing-adr

Writes a new ADR to `{{ .layout.adrDir }}/NNNN-kebab-title.md` (status `Proposed`) and commits it. Scope each record to a single load-bearing commitment: one decision per ADR. See `{{ .layout.workflowRef }}` for the full lifecycle rules and `{{ .prefix }}-adr-lifecycle` for state transitions.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section when-to-invoke -->
## When to invoke

Per `{{ .layout.workflowRef }}`: load-bearing decisions only, one ADR per decision. A Decision commitment remains meaningful after implementation and passes the post-implementation and counterfactual tests; a mechanism belongs only when the ADR explains why the mechanism itself is load-bearing. Route implementation directives to the plan. Bugfixes and routine refactors do not need an ADR. When in doubt, consult the ADR guide rather than expanding the record into a task list.

